---
export const title = 'Video files';
export const order = 200;
---

<p>
  Any <code>src</code> that is not a YouTube or Vimeo link is a video file. It plays in the browser's
  own player, with its keyboard-accessible controls, and loads nothing until the person presses play
  (<code>preload="none"</code>). Put <code>&lt;track&gt;</code> elements in the video for captions
  and subtitles; give every video with speech captions.
</p>

<pre><code>&lt;wc-video src="/media/tour.mp4" poster="/media/tour.webp" label="Product tour"&gt;
  &lt;track kind="captions" src="/media/tour.en.vtt" srclang="en" label="English" default /&gt;
  &lt;track kind="subtitles" src="/media/tour.de.vtt" srclang="de" label="Deutsch" /&gt;
&lt;/wc-video&gt;</code></pre>

<h3>Accessibility</h3>
<p>
  The poster is one button named "Play: <em>label</em>", so a screen reader announces what will play.
  The player that replaces it takes <code>label</code> as its title and receives focus. Captions are
  the app's to provide: on YouTube and Vimeo in the video site's own settings, and for files with
  <code>&lt;track&gt;</code>.
</p>
